Combines the items of a list from the left, starting from an initial value. The input is the triple [f [init xs]]: f takes the pair [acc item] and gives the new accumulator, so fold of nil is init, and the result for [1 2 ~] is f of [f of [init 1] 2].
---

---
(fn p
  (letrec go
    (fn (acc l) (if (? l) acc (go ((head p) [acc (head l)]) (tail l))))
    (go (head (tail p)) (tail (tail p)))))
---
[(fn p (+ (head p) (tail p))) [0 [1 2 3 ~]]] => 6 fuel 100000
[(fn p (+ (head p) (tail p))) [7 ~]] => 7 fuel 100000
[(fn p [(tail p) (head p)]) [~ [1 2 ~]]] => [2 1 ~] fuel 100000
